-- scripts/dst/invariants_dst.ail
--
-- WI-A14 piece 1 acceptance, under ADR-001 D7.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- The shape of this suite, and why it is that shape
-- ============================================================================
--
-- ONE FIXTURE THAT MUST SURVIVE, and everything else is a single-field mutation
-- of it. S7 is the reason and it is the rule mutation testing structurally
-- cannot supply: C5's mutants prove a guard CAN fire; they cannot see a guard
-- that fires TOO MUCH, because every mutant still produces its own rule. Only a
-- fixture that must PASS can, and this project has lost two items to guards
-- that over-rejected while every mutant row was green.
--
-- S7's two halves are both EXECUTABLE here rather than described:
--
--   * `scenario_fixture_carries_every_protected_shape` — every one of D2's
--     seven interaction classes, all three outcome statuses, chunks present and
--     absent, a deadline-bearing class and a deadline-free one, all three tool
--     fault classes, a denial and an end-of-input on the approval channel, and
--     a returned trace carrying all three LedgerRecord constructors.
--   * `scenario_no_two_fixture_quantities_are_equal` — over the quantities the
--     CHECKS read, listed by name. Prose cannot do either: a fixture's coverage
--     drifts silently as the driver changes and the author is the last person
--     who will notice.
--
-- WHICH QUANTITIES ARE IN THE DISTINCTNESS SET, and why the others are not.
-- S7 asks for two different things — that every protected SHAPE be PRESENT, and
-- that no two QUANTITIES be equal — and conflating them produces a fixture
-- bloated with sixteen environment reads for no reason. The distinctness set is
-- the counts that AT LEAST TWO checks read and could therefore confuse:
-- compaction stages, provider interactions, faulted interactions, tool
-- interactions, checkpoints, approvals, decisions, chunks, wire records, total
-- interactions, total records. The four singleton classes (env read, clock
-- advance, random draw, extension effect) appear once each purely for SHAPE
-- coverage, and no check compares their counts to anything — so they are
-- asserted PRESENT and deliberately left out of the distinctness set. Stated
-- rather than left to be inferred from the numbers.
--
-- EVERY MUTATION ROW ASSERTS ITS OWN RULE, never a non-empty finding list.
-- Cluster 12 measured what that buys: thirteen decode rows survived a
-- corruption that would have made eleven of them report a DIFFERENT rule, and
-- because each asserted its own, those eleven would have gone loudly red rather
-- than passing on the wrong evidence.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- The fixture is CONSTRUCTED, not swept, and that is cluster 12's limit
-- ============================================================================
--
-- A13 stage 4's technique — sweep the generator and filter on the obligations —
-- cannot supply this fixture. The generator provably cannot reach every shape
-- the invariant set protects: it produces no provider fault and no provider
-- latency (cluster 10's correction 2), `approval_deadline_exceeded` is
-- structurally unreachable, and no run of any kind produces a non-empty stream
-- emission log until Milestone B. A swept fixture would carry exactly the
-- shapes today's generator happens to produce, and the branches for the rest
-- would not be pinned — they would be ABSENT, which reads identically to
-- unchanged. Sweep-and-filter selects among things that exist; it cannot cover
-- a space the producer does not reach.

